diagnosis_text:
The routes the monitoring operator identified as missing — 17.1.x.x/32 loopbacks, 67.0.0.0/8, and 70.0.0.0/8 — are fully present in R1's OSPF routing table and installed in the FIB. R7's ospfd has been running continuously since container start (12:18:23), formed its OSPF adjacency with R6 at 12:19:08, and the FRR log contains no subsequent events (no crashes, no neighbor drops, no restarts). Watchfrr shows no process restart. No fault-injection script or ACL exists on R7 or on any router in the R7→R6→R4→R3→R1 forwarding path. The ~3-minute age difference between R13's EIGRP-redistributed routes (one hop via R11 in area 0.0.0.3) and R7's inter-area OSPF routes (four hops, two area boundaries, Type-3 LSA generation at R4) is consistent with normal differential convergence after lab startup in a multi-area OSPF topology. The ticket was almost certainly raised during the initial convergence window when R7's routes had not yet propagated to R1. R13 is intentionally EIGRP-only (watchfrr excludes ospfd; frr.conf has an explicit EIGRP design comment); its routes reach R1 correctly via redistribution at R11. Minor non-fault anomalies exist elsewhere (R12 ospfd running unconfigured, R8 orphaned area 0.0.0.2) but neither affects the R7 region prefixes. No corrective action is required for the reported symptom; routes are stable and the monitoring screen should clear on its next refresh cycle.
=== END ===